<%= render(@layout.new(field: @field)) do |component| %>
  <% component.with_label do %>
    <%= label %>
  <% end %>

  <% component.with_value do %>
    <% if label != "FAST Subject Headings:" %>
      <%= @field.render %>
    <% elsif label == "FAST Subject Headings:"%>
      <%#
        DIRECT RENDERING: FAST Subject Headings in Index/Search Results
        
        PURPOSE:
        Render subject_fast_ssim field values in search results/index pages
        with direct template rendering instead of render_async gem.
        
        WHY DIRECT RENDERING:
        render_async gem requires jQuery available on window object, which causes
        failures in both /catalog and /spotlight contexts. Results in empty async
        divs with no content. Solution: fetch term definitions directly in template
        using OclcSubjectFastService and render as hyperlinked facets.
        
        FIELD STRUCTURE:
        - @field.document: Solr document hash containing field values
        - @field.field_name: String "subject_fast_ssim" (Solr field name)
        - @field.field_value: Array of FAST URIs for display
        
        RENDERING LOGIC:
        1. Extract subject_fast URLS from Solr document
        2. For each URL, fetch term definition using OclcSubjectFastService
        3. Render as clickable facet link with context-aware base path
        4. Use current_exhibit to generate appropriate /catalog or /spotlight path
        
        DEPENDENCIES:
        - OclcSubjectFastService: Validates FAST URIs and fetches definitions
        - current_exhibit: Helper to detect Spotlight context
        
        DIFFERENCES FROM SHOW PAGE (_field_subject_fast.erb):
        - Index context: Uses field_value array directly (already extracted by Blacklight)
        - Show context: Receives subject_name parameter passed from template
        - Both: Use same context-aware facet URL pattern
        - Both: Use same OclcSubjectFastService for term fetching
      %>
      <%#
        DIRECT RENDERING: FAST Subject Headings in Index/Search Results
        
        PURPOSE:
        Render subject_fast_ssim field values in search results/index pages
        with direct template rendering instead of render_async gem.
        
        WHY DIRECT RENDERING:
        render_async gem requires jQuery available on window object, which causes
        failures in both /catalog and /spotlight contexts. Results in empty async
        divs with no content. Solution: fetch term definitions directly in template
        using OclcSubjectFastService and render as hyperlinked facets.
        
        FIELD STRUCTURE:
        - @field.document: Solr document hash containing field values
        - @field.field_name: String "subject_fast_ssim" (Solr field name)
        - @field.values: Array of FAST URIs for display
        
        RENDERING LOGIC:
        1. Extract subject_fast URLS from Solr document
        2. For each URL, fetch term definition using OclcSubjectFastService
        3. Render as clickable facet link with context-aware base path
        4. Use view_context.current_exhibit to generate appropriate /catalog or /spotlight path
        
        DEPENDENCIES:
        - OclcSubjectFastService: Validates FAST URIs and fetches definitions
        - view_context.current_exhibit: Helper to detect Spotlight context (accessed through component's view context)
        
        DIFFERENCES FROM SHOW PAGE (_field_subject_fast.erb):
        - Index context: Uses field.values array directly (already extracted by Blacklight)
        - Show context: Receives subject_name parameter passed from template
        - Both: Use same context-aware facet URL pattern
        - Both: Use same OclcSubjectFastService for term fetching
      %>
      <% (@field.values || []).each do |url| %>
        <% service = OclcSubjectFastService.new(url) %>
        <% term_data = service.uri_check ? service.fast_data : url %>
        <% exhibit = @view_context.respond_to?(:current_exhibit) ? @view_context.current_exhibit : nil %>
        <% facet_base = exhibit ? "/spotlight/#{exhibit.slug}/catalog" : '/catalog' %>
        <span itemprop=""><%= link_to term_data, "#{facet_base}?f%5Bsubject_fast_ssim%5D%5B%5D=#{url}", class: "show-page-label" %></span>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>